## 🎤 12. SOC Interview Questions

**Q1. What is Windows Event ID 4688?**  
It records that a new process was created.

**Q2. Why might the command line be missing from Event ID 4688?**  
Command-line inclusion may not be enabled, or the information may not be available for that event.

**Q3. What is Event ID 4698?**  
It records the creation of a scheduled task.

**Q4. Why correlate process creation with scheduled-task events?**  
It can help establish whether a task was created and whether related processes subsequently ran.

**Q5. Does an unusual parent-child process relationship prove malware?**  
No. It is an indicator to investigate in context.

**Q6. What should you do if no Event ID 4688 records appear?**  
Check the audit policy, log access, event availability, and whether the test generated a new event.

